    "summary": "Solid late‑1973 set with standout Casey Jones jam and crisp China>Rider",
    "blurb": "Features a strong mix of late‑1973 material highlighted by a fiery Casey Jones → Jam → One More Saturday Night suite and an inspired China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider transition. The soundboard source offers clear, well‑balanced audio despite being a partial recording. Energy runs medium‑high throughout the set.",
    "review": "December 10, 1973 at Charlotte Coliseum finds the Dead in fine form, delivering a tight first set of classics like Bertha and Playing In The Band before launching into a second half that really shines. The standout moment comes when Casey Jones rolls out into an unplanned jam that segues into One More Saturday Night – a high‑octane burst that captures the band’s spontaneous spirit even though the recording ends there. Later, the China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider pairing is played with crisp interplay and Keith’s tasteful organ fills, showcasing the group’s tight chemistry during this late‑1973 era. While the release is only a partial soundboard capture, its good‑quality mix lets the nuances of Jerry’s lead lines and Phil’s supportive bass shine through, making it a worthwhile listen for fans seeking a taste of the band’s late‑year energy.",
